FL-024 part 2 landed as 62d6a81 (main and master): the metric overlay. The Studio's window now draws text, as triangles on FrankenManim's 3D route.

What it does:
- flife-manim `hud` lays text out with fmn-text, the bundled IBM Plex Sans. It flattens each quadratic to within 0.2 px of its curve, nests the contours by containment, and ear-clips each ink contour with its holes using fmn-geom.
  - The text stops at 6,144 vertices and 6,144 triangles, half as much again as the Studio's longest overlay at 2x (3,990 / 3,778).
  - A glyph the triangulator refuses is left out and counted.
  - Both crates were already in the lockfile through fmn at the pinned rev.
- The text sits on a black plate at 0.6 opacity in the top-left corner. It is drawn last and unlit, through the camera's own pixel-to-scene map, so pan and zoom don't move it. adopt() rebuilds it on any viewport change.
- WorldView::enable_overlay charges the text's ceiling under FL-043 whether or not text is shown:
  - reserved: two texts, plates and meshes;
  - preparation: the triangles;
  - frame: two draws.
  Studio::open enables it before memory admission: 13.0 MiB at 3840x2160.
- The lines are composed from the session's state:
  - "running · tick 1,024" or "paused";
  - the clock reading while show_clock_telemetry is set ("128 ticks/s · 1.00× real time · 60 fps");
  - "<mapping> mapping · <brush> brush · organism N".

Evidence (headless, macOS arm64; no window opened):
- flife-manim tests/hud.rs, 7 tests, each oracle independent of the triangulation:
  - flattening within 0.2 px (4,097 samples × 6 curves);
  - all 95 printable ASCII characters plus ×·–—…° at ems of 13 and 26 px: at about 12.8M grid points, being inside a triangle equals a nonzero winding number of the flattened contours;
  - line pitch 1.2 em, and spaces take no ink;
  - both budget ceilings bind;
  - the camera map agrees with the view across 3 shapes × 4 viewports (to 1e-9);
  - the charges are exact, and the draws come last in order;
  - a CPU render with Hg8 at 80 px: byte-identical outside the plate, ink at sRGB 231 ±1.5, the plate at 0.4× linear light ±1.5.
- flife-studio tests/overlay.rs (2): the exact strings, and the longest overlay set whole within two thirds of the budget. tests/admission.rs builds its views as Studio::open does, and the overlay adds exactly its view terms.
- flife-cli memory_admission: a 4K view at 2x, with the longest text laid out twice and two zooms, peaks at 9.87 of 12.46 MiB reserved.
- Planted mutants: 17 of 17 non-equivalent caught, after one test fix. O5 (the vertex ceiling never binds) survived the first run, and a hole-free budget text was added. O3 (the ray cast in the other direction) is equivalent.
- Gates: fmt; clippy -D warnings on both feature sets; rustdoc -D warnings; workspace tests 113 binaries, 602 passed, 0 failed.

